<title>FRANCE: Forecaster sees flat European car market to 2000.</title>
<headline>Forecaster sees flat European car market to 2000.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris chamber of commerce's economic research division, COE, has forecast that the European car market would stay flat between 1998-2000 after posting 2.5 percent growth this year.</p>
<p>It said French and German car sales were expected to grow one percent annually from 1998, but would fall slightly in Italy, after incentive-driven growth there this year, and in Britain.</p>
<p>Spain would show the most vigorous growth of three percent a year, the COE said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
